# desk_ward.dlg
# The desk scene. This one runs in the close-up view, so it can use @portrait
# and mood tags. It is also the reference example for the whole format:
# choices, conditions, counters, stage directions and a branching ending all
# appear here.

:: start
@music tense
> The chair is new. The file is not.
Choi: ...
Choi @tired: Nineteen hours signed in, and he leaves this on my desk.

+ [Open the file] -> open_file
+ [Leave it closed] -> leave_it
+ [Ask Ward about it first] if trust_ward >= 1 -> ask_first

:: open_file
set read_case_file = true
> Twelve pages. Four of them are photocopies of the same page.
Choi: Somebody wanted this to look thicker than it is.
@portrait right ward flat
Ward: You opened it.
Choi: You left it out.
-> confrontation

:: leave_it
> You put your hand flat on the cover and leave it there.
Choi: Not tonight.
set suspicion += 1
@portrait right ward flat
Ward: Smart.
Ward @flat: Or slow. Hard to tell from here.
-> parting

:: ask_first
@portrait right ward amused
Choi: This is yours.
Ward: It's the department's. I just carried it.
Choi @wary: Then carry it back.
set trust_ward += 1
-> confrontation

:: confrontation
Ward: Ask me the question you actually want to ask.

+ [Why is your name on every page?] -> question_name
+ [Who told you to bring it to me?] -> question_order
+ [Nothing. Close the file.] -> parting

:: question_name
Choi: Why is your name on every page?
Ward @tense: Because I was there.
set suspicion += 1
-> weigh

:: question_order
Choi: Who told you to bring it to me?
Ward: Nobody tells me anything. That's the job.
set trust_ward += 1
-> weigh

:: weigh
# A branch on accumulated state rather than on a single choice. This is where
# the numbers a scene has been quietly collecting finally pay off.
if trust_ward >= 2 -> trusted
if suspicion >= 2 -> suspicious
-> parting

:: trusted
Ward @quiet: Choi. When you write this up, leave the times out.
Choi: Why.
Ward: Because I'm asking.
set told_truth = true
-> parting

:: suspicious
Ward @cold: Write it however you like.
> He is already at the door.
-> parting

:: parting
@music none
> The file stays on the desk. So does the question.
end
